    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636-a1">

                <pb facs="0751" n="III" xml:id="pgIII"/>

                <head>Mr. Martin to Mr. Adams,.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartlepool,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honorable Sir:</hi> In forwarding to you the
                    accompanying resolution, I may just take the opportunity to state my belief that
                    there does not exist in the minds of the masses of my fellow-countrymen those
                    pro-southern proclivities which American citizens, with much ill blood, give us
                    credit for. Wherever there are bad men, there we shall find bad things of all
                    kinds, pro-slavery among the rest. We have such in this country, of course, but,
                    really, all the world must allow that they bear a very small proportion to the
                    whole population.</p>
                <p>The receipt of this will oblige, yours, obediently,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. MARTIN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—You are at liberty to make what use you think proper of this
                        communication.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d636-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d636-a1-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
